anner.   Only users who have access to a private folder can access the widgets that include a private folder.  This feature is already available on preview systems.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\",461\n404,\"--- Record 3691 ---\nComponent: Cloud Portal Service\nEnvironment: Neo\nTitle: End Of Maintenance for SAP Cloud Portal service, version 1.0 (Neo Environment)\nDescription: SAP Cloud Portal service, version 1.0 on the Neo Environment will reach the status End-of-Maintenance on 31st December 2023.  This version of SAP Cloud Portal service will be deprecated on 25th January 2024, and from that point on, access to this service won’t be possible.  SAP Cloud Portal service, version 2.0 on the Neo Environment, released in December 2015, is not affected by this change.    Note  To verify which version you’re using, please note the differences in the site URL:     Scenario  Version 1.0  Version 2.0        Design time  URL ends with /portal/index.html  URL contains adminspace      Runtime  URL contains /portal/cloud-portal/index.html  URL contains dispatcher      \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: Deprecated\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2023-12-31\nValid as Of: 2023-12-31\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3692 ---\nComponent: SAP Conversational AI\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Tenant Header Configuration Endpoint\nDescription: As of June 2023, /auth/v1/update_tenant_security_header_toggle has been deprectaed. For more information, see API documentation.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: Deprecated\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2023-07-05\nValid as Of: 2023-12-31\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3693 ---\nComponent: SAP Conversational AI\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Tenant Security Headers\nDescription: As of June 2023, you must configure tenant security headers for your enterprise tenant. You cannot set security header toggle for your enterprise tenant to false using the Tenant Header Configuration endpoint. See Configure Tenant Security Headers.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2023-07-05\nValid as Of: 2023-12-31\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3694 ---\nComponent: SAP Build Work Zone, advanced edition\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Aligned Tile Behavior\nDescription: Until now, certain application tiles such as Dynamic tiles and tiles with custom images, behaved differently when accessed from a workpage rather than through the Applications page. This behavior has been aligned and now all application tiles behave the same no matter where they are accessed from.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2023-12-21\nValid as Of: 2023-12-28\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3695 ---\nComponent: SAP Build Work Zone, advanced edition\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Integration with Central Notification\nDescription: Site administrators can choose whether to use the default notification mechanism available in their site, or to enable the integration with central notification, and show notifications from multiple notification providers. As part of this change, part of the notifications will be migrated to the Task Center.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2023-12-21\nValid as Of: 2023-12-28\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3696 ---\nComponent: SAP Build Work Zone, advanced edition\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Menu Workpage Widgets Can Reference Contents From Workspaces\nDescription: Widgets in workpages ,which are part of the site menu, can reference content from any public or private workspace. Supported widgets are Multimedia, Image, Poll, Slide Show, and Rotating Banner widgets.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Tech